From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:45:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(transport): per-run model request pacer from a
 shared sliding-window ledger

RHOAI3 Stage 080 (architect review R2): the declared request allowance of a
run must be enforced, not only checked. When RHOAI3_REQUEST_BUDGET=<n>/<s>
and RHOAI3_REQUEST_LEDGER=<path> are set, every model HTTP request any
Hermes process of the run sends takes one slot from an append-only,
flock-protected ledger shared by all processes and surviving restarts.
Unset => disabled, behaviour unchanged.

- agent/request_pacer.py: ledger and sliding window. One acquisition waits
  at most RHOAI3_REQUEST_BUDGET_MAX_WAIT (default 900 s) IN TOTAL (elapsed
  monotonic time, at least the sum of its sleeps), so a competitor that
  keeps winning expiring slots cannot extend the wait; it stops at once
  when the first predicted slot is already beyond the allowance. Exhaustion
  raises RequestBudgetExhausted with a named STOP MODEL_REQUEST_BUDGET
  message (worded to avoid the dispatcher's quota/auth respawn-blocker
  pattern) before anything is sent.
- Enforcement: an httpx request event hook attached at the OpenAI client
  construction choke points (agent_runtime_helpers primary client;
  auxiliary_client sync, async and Vertex clients), so each HTTP attempt,
  including every Hermes and SDK retry and stream reconnect, takes exactly
  one slot (POST only).
- Main loop: reserve() takes the attempt's slot before the API call, outside
  the stream stale detector, touching worker activity; the transport hook
  consumes that reservation instead of waiting again, so one total-wait
  bound covers both. Exhaustion is never retried and ends the turn with
  model_stop=request_budget, recorded by the shared kanban worker-stop
  recorder as a failed run.
- A wait inside the transport hook (auxiliary call, stream reconnect) is not
  a stale stream: the streaming watchdog treats an active pacer wait as
  activity. A stream attempt registers a cancel check, so a cancelled or
  interrupted attempt aborts its wait without taking a slot or sending.
